# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets / generated config
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# google-services.json IS committed (see android/app/) — Firebase
# docs explicitly state these client identifiers are not secret. The
# API key inside is hardware-restricted to com.bobaplaybook.app +
# the SHA-1 fingerprints registered in Firebase Console, so a leaked
# key can't be used by other apps. (Industry-standard posture; iOS
# Apple-style equivalent files are also committed.)
#
# DO NOT commit:
#   - upload-key keystore (~/.android/boba-upload.jks) — handled by *.jks above
#   - keystore passwords — keep in ~/.gradle/gradle.properties (NOT here)
#   - Supabase service role key — Worker-only secret, never bundled in app
#   - Play Service Account JSON for CI — GitHub Actions secret only
#   - Any *.p8 / *.p12 / *.pem private key

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Bundled assets — synced from /assets/data/ + iOS Fonts/ via
# scripts/sync_shared_assets.sh. We DO commit them (the iOS bundle
# is already in git at BOBAPlaybook/display-cards.json; mirroring
# the same posture keeps Android devs from needing to run the
# sync before they can open the project). The Gradle preBuild task
# refreshes them on every build so they stay current.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# (no exclusion here — see scripts/sync_shared_assets.sh)

